(ARG-47: a number flag token beyond the range of a number is not a number
 ("The whole number must fit in a number", LANGUAGE.md:2233-2235), so the
 flag holds its default and the error flag is raised (LANGUAGE.md:
 4926-4928). retries has no default and holds 0; patience has default 5
 and keeps it.
 Up to vox 0.4.15 the value wrapped modulo 2^64 instead
 (99999999999999999999 read as 7766279631452241919) and this probe
 printed "retries is 7766279631452241919": Discrepancy 4, resolved by
 vox #281. Re-recorded 2026-10-13 on vox main a0a2ecc.
 Only the first handler runs: Parse flags converts both tokens and raises
 the flag once, and the first On error catches and clears it.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-47.vox -o p && ./p -r 99999999999999999999 -p 99999999999999999999
 Args: -r 99999999999999999999 -p 99999999999999999999
 expected output:
   reading retries errored
   retries is 0
   patience is 5
)
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
a flag called patience is "-p" or "--patience", it is a number with default 5.
Parse flags.

a number called seen is retries.
On error print "reading retries errored".
Print "retries is {seen}".
a number called waited is patience.
On error print "reading patience errored".
Print "patience is {waited}".
